{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>I see him, but not now.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): he prophesied concerning David, peace be upon him. And he said 'but not now,' for this prophecy came four hundred years later, for it is he who struck the corners of Moab and crushed all the children of Seth — and Seth was the principal progeny of man. Or he may mean 'children of Seth' in the sense of foundations, as in (Psalms 11) ״כי השתות״, meaning he will crush and demolish the cities. 'And Edom shall be his possession' — we find concerning David that his hand prevailed over Edom and Seir. 'There shall step down a ruler from Jacob' — a ruler shall arise from Jacob. 'And destroy the remnant from the city' — that is, from every city of idolatry; and this is David, concerning whom it is written (I Kings 11:16): ״עד הכרית כל זכר באדום״. And Rashi, of blessed memory, interpreted: 'There shall step down a ruler from Jacob' — this is the Messiah, concerning whom it is said (Psalms 72:8) ״וירד מים עד ים״; and 'and destroy the remnant' — this is what is written (Obadiah 1:18) ״ולא יהיה שריד לבית עשו״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: 'I see him but not now' — this is David; 'I behold him, but it is not near' — this is King Messiah; 'There shall step a star from Jacob' — this is David; 'And a scepter shall arise from Israel' — this is King Messiah; 'And he shall strike the corners of Moab' — this is David, concerning whom it is written (II Samuel 8:2) ״ויך את מואב וימדדם בחבל״; 'And he shall crush all the children of Seth' — this is King Messiah, concerning whom it is written (Psalms 72:8) ״וירד מים עד ים״; 'And Edom shall be his possession' — this is David, as it is said (II Samuel 8:14) ״ויהי כל אדום עבדים לדוד״; 'And Edom shall be a possession, and Seir shall be a possession of his enemies, and Israel does valiantly' — this is King Messiah, as it is said (Obadiah 1:21) ״ועלו מושיעים בהר ציון לשפוט את הר עשו״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The citation תהלים י\"א is Psalms 11:3 (כי השתות); exact verse number not specified in the Hebrew. The Hebrew text interleaves Rashi's interpretation of the Messianic reading alongside the plain sense; the translation follows the structure faithfully."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:55.696415462Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}